BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meanwhile in Vermont... Where do we show up in our nation's foundi
 ng documents?
DTSTART:20260923T150000
DTEND:20260923T163000
DTSTAMP:20260923T152847Z
UID:3fc61cc3392049320206eff0188047@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:A 250th anniversary panel discussion: When the Continental Con
 gress signed the Declaration of Independence\, Vermont did not exist. The 
 area was called the New Hampshire Grants and was already embroiled in conf
 lict with the colonies of New York and New Hampshire over land ownership a
 nd government jurisdiction. Learn about this time in history and the refer
 ences to Vermont that appear in primary-source documents in the U.S. Gover
 nment Information Collection at Howe Library. Join us for a panel discussi
 on with: Alec Ewald - Professor of Political Science\, UVM. Alexandra Garr
 ett - Assistant Professor of History\, Saint Michael's College and Revolut
 ionary War Historian for Vermont's 250th Anniversary Commission. Angela Gr
 ove - Director of the Ethan Allen Homestead Museum. Trina Magi\, Coordinat
 or of the Federal Depository Library Collection and Map Room at Howe Libra
 ry\, UVM.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:University of Vermont Howe Library\, Atrium\, 538 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/meanwhile-
 in-vermont-where-do-we-show-up-in-our-nations-founding-documents-02-09-202
 6-14-46-15
END:VEVENT
