DESCRIPTION:Get ready to laugh as you move to modern music--in a square. M
 odern square dancing is a low impact exercise for body and brain. Your soc
 ial life will instantly double when you come dance with our friendly inclu
 sive club! Experienced dancers help the new dancers. There are snacks. Wha
 t's not to like? First two sessions (9/16 and 9/23) FREE\, only $7 (less w
 ith a prepay) per workshop in regular session. Session goes until about Fe
 bruary 2027 to learn all the square dance calls!\n\nSources: Vermont Publi
 c
LOCATION:Lothrop Elementary School\, 3447 U.S. Route 7
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/modern-squ
 are-dance-series-08-09-2026-21-16-43
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SafeArt Welcome Party
DTSTART:20260923T180000
DTEND:20260923T200000
DTSTAMP:20260923T152847Z
UID:0ca7761b4b773bc53237674bcc358a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate our new partnership with SafeArt\, meet their t
 eam\, enjoy some food\, connect with neighbors\, and help shape exciting n
 ew community programs! SafeArt is a team of trauma-informed practitioners 
 who use creative expression to cultivate community wellness and positive s
 ocial change. We want to hear from YOU! What kinds of experiences would yo
 u love to see in our community? Whether you have a big idea or simply want
  to meet your neighbors\, come join the conversation! Bring a friend\, bri
 ng a neighbor\, and bring your ideas. Together\, we can create something m
 eaningful\, creative\, and connected. Parking located across the street at
  37 Academy Lane. McIndoes Academy Event Center\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/safeart-we
 lcome-party-13-08-2026-14-41-11
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shostakovich Against Stalin: The War Symphonies
DTSTART:20260923T183000
DTEND:20260923T210000
DTSTAMP:20260923T152847Z
UID:74a3535a03060d453a14aa2d3d786f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join OCM Artistic Director Doug Anderson for his opening remar
 ks about this timely festival\, celebrating the tenacity of the human spir
 it. The reception will be followed by Shostakovich Against Stalin: The War
  Symphonies\, a powerful documentary exploring Dmitri Shostakovich's warti
 me symphonies against the backdrop of Stalin's Soviet Union. Weaving toget
 her remarkable archival footage\, moving personal testimony\, and stirring
  performances\, this acclaimed film examines how Shostakovich's wartime sy
 mphonies came to symbolize artistic courage and resilience in the face of 
 totalitarian rule. Town Hall Theater\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/shostakovi
 ch-against-stalin-the-war-symphonies-15-09-2026-13-39-40
END:VEVENT
